.TH ASLGC 1 "November 2026" "aslgc 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aslgc \- a simple Linux Git client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aslgc
[\fIOPTION\fR]... [\fIPATH\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aslgc
is a graphical Git client. It shows repositories in tabs with a commit graph,
lets you stage whole files, hunks or single lines, and runs branch, merge,
rebase, stash, fetch, pull and push operations. All operations are carried out
by the
.BR git (1)
command line, so hooks, signing and configuration apply as usual.
.PP
Each
.I PATH
is opened as a repository tab. Without arguments the tabs of the previous
session are restored.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of the options and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ASLGC_GIT
Path of the git executable to use instead of the one found on
.BR PATH .
.TP
.B ASLGC_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID
Client ID of a GitHub OAuth App used for browser sign-in, overriding the value
chosen at build time.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/aslgc/aslgc.conf
Settings: open tabs, recent repositories, window layout and the list of
signed-in accounts. Account tokens are kept in the system keyring
(Secret Service or KWallet), not in this file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1)
